## Application
These plenum boxes are designed to connect round air terminal devices (round diffusers, swirl diffusers, circulation diffusers, disc valves, nozzles) to the ductwork in supply and exhaust ventilation, air conditioning or air heating systems.

## Design and materials
Made of 0.7 mm galvanised steel. The connection can be either on the side or on the top. The inlet spigot D1 is made for a nipple connection, with an outer diameter 3 mm smaller than nominal. The outlet spigot D2 must be 2-3 mm larger than the connection diameter of the air terminal device.

## Manufacturing
Made to installation dimensions AxA; the height H must be at least d+50 mm (for a side connection). For a top connection, the height can be as low as 100 mm.

## Order example and installation
**Plenum box VD 500х500х200h/LC/Perf/TM/Izol/DK d-125/VR d-127 (RAL 9005М/RAL 9005М)**

500x500 - plenum dimensions (but not less than D2+20);

200h - plenum height (but not less than D1+50);

LC – side connection (TC – top connection);

Perf – perforated plate inside the plenum for even distribution of the airflow;

TM – traverse bar (a strip with holes) for fixing round diffusers;

Izol – acoustic insulation;

DK - butterfly damper (RZ - adjustable damper operated from inside, VR - plain spigot);

d-125 - connection diameter 125 mm (actual 122 (-3 mm));

RAL 9005M – painted black inside and outside;

To make it easier to fix the plenum boxes to building structures, mounting brackets are provided on the side faces.

## Scope of supply
Can be supplied with additional elements (options):

- perforated plate;
- butterfly damper instead of a plain spigot;
- adjustable damper operated from inside;
- traverse bar;
- powder coating;
- acoustic insulation.

