## Application
Plenum boxes are designed to connect air terminal devices (linear slot diffusers and grilles) to the ductwork in supply and exhaust ventilation, air conditioning or air heating systems.

## Design and materials
Made of galvanised steel. The connection can be either on the side or on the top. The inlet spigot is made for a nipple connection, with an outer diameter 3 mm smaller than nominal.

They have a "correct" shape with a mixing chamber that reduces air velocity and distributes air more evenly along the entire length. Pre-installed slats with holes and cut threads allow the linear slot diffusers to be fixed with screws. The maximum length is 2.4 m, and the units can be assembled into one continuous line: the first plenum has no right-hand end cap (PS-L), the second and subsequent ones have no end caps on either side (PS-C), and the last one has only a left-hand end cap (PS-R). For joining, a connecting slat with holes is additionally fitted to one of the plenums at the open end, while matching holes are pre-drilled in the other. Assembly is done by sliding the plenum onto the slat, aligning the holes and fixing with rivets or self-tapping screws.

For lengths over 1200 mm, two or more spigots are recommended for a more even air supply along the entire length of the diffuser.

## Manufacturing
Made to installation dimensions AxB (there must be a 2–5 mm clearance between the diffuser's installation dimensions and the plenum connection dimensions); the height H must be at least d+F (standard 50 mm, but not less) +20 mm (for a side connection).

For example, with a d125 spigot the minimum height H is 195 mm (50+125+20). For a top connection, the height can be as low as 150 mm (F50+100).

## Order example and installation
**Slot plenum PS-G=500 170×1505/С=270/F=40/H=170h/LC/Izol/RZ d-100 (RAL 9005М/RAL 9005М)**

PS — slot plenum, closed at both ends (for assembly in a line: first — PS-L, middle — PS-C, last — PS-R);

G=500 — distance from the left edge to the partition inside the plenum that separates the ventilation and air conditioning flows;

170 — plenum connection width (+2–3 mm to the width of the linear slot diffuser);

1505 — slot plenum length (+5 mm to the length of the linear slot diffuser);

C=270 — chamber width (standard A+100 mm);

F=40 — installation height of the linear slot diffuser;

H=170h — overall plenum height (formula: F + connection d + 20);

SC — side connection (TC — top connection);

Izol — internal acoustic insulation;

RZ d-100 — adjustable damper operated from inside;

(RAL 9005М) — painted black inside and outside.

For easy fixing to building structures, mounting brackets are provided on the side faces.

## Scope of supply
Optional extras:

- butterfly damper for adjusting the supply air volume;
- adjustable internal damper (perforated blade, handle accessible inside the plenum);
- oval spigots for reduced height (connection with flexible ducts only);
- special d-63, d-75 or d-90 openings for connecting FlexiVent semi-rigid ducts;
- d-75 or d-90 openings for connecting AeroFlex semi-rigid ducts;
- internal insulation for noise reduction;
- perimeter flange;
- powder coating inside/outside in any RAL colour.

